UMI MIKIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUROKI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA MASATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OHOSAWA TAKAYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OSHIKI MITSUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SANO SHUZOU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHARA, SHOSAKU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IZUMI, MIKIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUROKI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHOSAWA, TAKAYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OSHIKI, MITSUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SANO, SHUZOU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A two-dimensionally arrayed probe (device packaging structure) which comprises a multilayer device as a piezoelectric ceramic vibration device and of which only the multilayer device can be replaced separately if defective and repaired if its connection is defective. A multilayer electronic part which is suitable for realizing such a device packaging structure includes a multilayer chip device having a surface electrode, an internal electrode, and a back electrode, and a flexible board stuck on one side of the chip device. Every other electrodes, in the multilayer direction, of the chip device are electrically connected with each other through an electrode pattern of the flexible board to form two electrode groups. The ends of the electrode pattern of the flexible board are used as two external connection electrodes electrically connected with the two electrode groups.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne une sonde à jeu d'éléments bi-dimensionnelle (structure de conditionnement) qui comprend un dispositif multicouche jouant le rôle de dispositif piézo-électrique céramique à vibration dont seul le dispositif multicouche peut être remplacé séparément en cas de défaillance, ou réparé en cas de connexion défectueuse. Cette invention concerne également un composant électronique multicouche qui permet de réaliser une telle structure de conditionnement et qui se compose d'un dispositif multicouche à puce comprenant une électrode de surface, une électrode interne et une électrode arrière, ainsi qu'un circuit souple collé sur l'un des côtés du dispositif à puce. Toutes les autres électrodes (dans le sens multicouche) du dispositif à puce sont connectées électriquement entre elles via un motif d'électrodes sur le circuit flexible et forment deux groupes d'électrodes. Les extrémités du motif d'électrodes sur le circuit souple constituent deux électrodes de connexion externes reliées aux deux groupes d'électrodes.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>